  "body": "Found in the review of PR #2904 (part 1 of #917). PR #2904 does not fix these two items.\n\n**1. Sheets have no heal and no integrity check.**\n- A sheet (`SHELL_BASED_SURFACE_MODEL`) does not go through `build_record` in `crates/kernel/src/solidcore_step.rs`.\n- Thus a sheet gets no heal, no integrity check and no vertex-gap check.\n- It lands as a whole model with open sides. The import does not set `open`.\n- This agrees with the old reader. But a gap between two faces inside a sheet now has no check and no note.\n- Expected: a note for each sheet that has open sides inside it (a gap between its own faces), or a refusal by name.\n\n**2. The hole line can name no face.**\n- `crates/geometry/src/step.rs:101` writes `hole(&label, faces, &open.left_out)`.\n- If `partial_mesh` returns an empty `left_out`, the hole line names no face.\n- The model still lands as incomplete, so this is conservative. But the line does not tell the user which face is missing.\n- Expected: a line that says that no face was named, or a refusal by name.\n\nDone means:\n- A sheet with an inner gap gets a named note (or refusal), pinned by a test.\n- An empty `left_out` gives a clear hole line (or a refusal), pinned by a test.\n\nRefs #917\n",
